<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Courland and Semigallia (1918)</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Mitau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">German client state proclaimed by Courland's Baltic German nobles in 1918, which offered its ducal crown to Kaiser Wilhelm II.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Under German occupation, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a> Landesrat, a council dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-germans">Baltic German</a> nobles, proclaimed on 8 March 1918 the restoration of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-courland-and-semigallia">Duchy of Courland and Semigallia</a>, covering the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/governorate-of-courland">Governorate of Courland</a>. It offered the ducal crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> recognised the duchy on 15 March.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The duchy had no real government of its own and depended on the German military administration that had replaced <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ober-ost">Ober Ost</a>. Its leaders planned German settlement and close union with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvians">Latvians</a>, the great majority of the population, were excluded from its councils and rejected it.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In autumn 1918 the duchy was to join the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-baltic-duchy">United Baltic Duchy</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany's</a> defeat in November ended the scheme. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-latvia">Republic of Latvia</a>, proclaimed on 18 November 1918, took over its territory after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvian-war-of-independence">War of Independence</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-courland-and-semigallia-1918.jpg" alt="Duchy of Courland and Semigallia (1918)" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Courland_(state).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mitau</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheran Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Latvian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/latvia">Latvia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Duchy of Courland (1918), Herzogtum Kurland und Semgallen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=duchy-of-courland-and-semigallia-1918" aria-label="Duchy of Courland and Semigallia (1918) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5193 253 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Courland and Semigallia (1918) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5513 509L5513 509M5513 509L5300 622M5513 509L5520 501"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5513 509h0M5300 622h0M5520 501h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5513 509h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5513 509h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=duchy-of-courland-and-semigallia-1918">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
